        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Split public LLM provider code from internal package",
        "summary": "Moved OpenAI-compatible and OpenRouter provider shims from `@codebuff/internal` to new public `@codebuff/llm-providers` package. Prevents SDK from depending on private server utilities while maintaining provider functionality. Updates architecture docs, package dependencies, and test mocks to reflect new structure. `packages/llm-providers/` now hosts forked AI SDK providers; `packages/internal/` retains only server-side utilities and database schema.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-14T23:57:35.533Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The SDK kit that outside developers use to talk to the AI no longer secretly leans on the company's private server-only code. The pieces that connect to OpenAI-style and OpenRouter AI endpoints were moved out of the hidden, server-restricted toolbox into a separate, publicly shared toolbox that the SDK is allowed to open. If you are an external developer pulling the Codebuff SDK into your own app, your project now depends on a clean, shareable package instead of tripping over internal plumbing; nothing about what the AI calls changes today, but the connection path is now safe for you to touch.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "35efda7ea14b",
        "at": "2026-09-17T20:26:52.110Z"
