        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add chat completion concurrency logging",
        "summary": "New `request-metrics.ts` module tracks active chat completion requests with sampled logging. Concurrency counters increment on start and decrement on completion, cancellation, or error, emitting structured metrics for host, PID, and duration. Streaming responses wrap the reader to detect stream end or failure, ensuring accurate lifecycle tracking.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-14T23:55:45.824Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "Your assistant can now quietly keep count of how many conversations are happening at the same time on each server. When you send a message, a counter ticks up, and when the reply finishes (or fails), it ticks back down, writing a brief note that includes which machine handled it, which conversation, and how long it took. If you run these servers yourself, you'll see a new kind of line in your logs roughly once every 20 requests, giving you a running tally of live traffic without flooding your system with data.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "b99cbc5ae32d",
        "at": "2026-09-17T20:26:50.491Z"
